deploy/aws-cdk/.venv
deploy/aws-cdk/cdk.out
deploy/aws-cdk/node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
.git
.venv
project.zip
results/*.png

# Exported image archives (`docker save ... | gzip > *.tar.gz`, e.g. from
# deploy's export-to-S3 scripts) land in the repo root on the build machine.
# Without this, rebuilding an image after one of these exists copies the
# previous export's multi-GB tarball straight into the next image — this bit
# spark-lean once already: an unrelated code fix triggered a rebuild while a
# prior 837MB spark-lean.tar.gz + 3.0GB ner-translate-server.tar.gz were
# still sitting in the build context, ballooning the "lean" image to 4.1GB.
*.tar.gz

# NOTE: wheelhouses (deploy/scripts/build_*_wheelhouse.sh output, under
# wheels/<pipeline>/) and .deb bundles (deploy/scripts/build_*_debs.sh
# output, under debs/<pipeline>/) are deliberately NOT excluded here.
# .dockerignore applies to the whole build context for every image built
# from this repo — excluding them here would also hide them from the
# targeted bind-mounts in deploy/Dockerfile.ner_translate{,_server} that
# need them to install this pipeline's deps. Instead, deploy/Dockerfile's
# `lean` and `final` stages skip both directories themselves (see their
# comments) when copying the app into those images, since those are the
# only stages that must never see them.

# Model weights are never baked into an image — they're mounted from the
# filesystem at container start (see docs/MODEL_CONTAINER_ISOLATION.md
# Option B). Without this, whatever happens to be sitting in models/weights/
# at build time (e.g. downloaded for local Tier 0/1 testing) gets copied
# into the image by `COPY . .`, silently bloating it by several GB and
# defeating the whole point of keeping images to just deps/packages/CUDA
# libs — this bit the very first AWS build of this image.
models/weights/*
!models/weights/.gitignore
!models/weights/README.md
